name			SurrealEngine
version			1.0.0-1
architecture	x86_64
summary 		"Surreal Engine"
description 	"Plays Unreal Tournament v436 and other supported games. Map and UT binary files required.

To Play:
Notes: 
v436 works really well. Anything higher may not work as well.
Works really well with nebula graphics stack.
Runs okay with default Mesa stack when not in fullscreen mode. 

1. Place UnrealTournament99 Game Folder in /boot/home/UnrealTournament_cd_436_patch as so
2. Open Terminal to /boot/system/apps/SurrealEngine/bin
3. Copy and Paste this into Terminal:
SE_DEBUG_FORCE_NULLTEX_WORLD=1 ./SurrealEngine /boot/home/UnrealTournament_cd_436_patch/

Main Issue:
1. Currently, map lighting textures is broken and that's why SE_DEBUG_FORCE_NULLTEX_WORLD=1 is used.
But hopefully will get that fixed soon :)

Other known issues: 
1. The main startup SDL window appears blank. Moving the mouse around or resizing window fixes that.
2. Exiting fullscreen and trying to move the game window sometimes jumps to bottom right corner.
3. Characters appear dark.
4. Networking is missing.
5. Fullscreen mode with default Haiku Mesa is a bit sluggish"
packager		"ablyss <SurrealEngine@epluribusunix.net>"
vendor			"epluribusunix.net Project"
licenses {
	"MIT"
}
copyrights {
	"2026 ablyss"
}
provides {
	SurrealEngine = 1.0.0-1	
}
requires {
	haiku
	libsdl2
	libsdl3
	openal
}	
urls {
	"https://github.com/ablyssx74/SurrealEngine"
}
